# Zeek packages installed by zeek/scripts/zeek_install_plugins.sh, with the ref to track for each.
#   This file is the input to scripts/zeek_packages_lock_refresh.sh, which resolves every entry to a
#   commit and writes zeek/zeek-packages.lock. The build installs only what's in the lock file, so
#   after editing this list, run the refresh script and review the lock file diff.
#
# Format (one per line; blank lines and # comments are ignored):
#   URL|ref|environment variables|method
#   URL     - the GitHub repository URL
#   ref     - optional branch, tag or commit to track; when empty, track the latest GitHub release,
#             else the highest version tag, else the default branch (matching zkg's own choice)
#   env     - optional semicolon-separated variables to set for the install
#             (e.g., CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug;HILTI_CXX_FLAGS=-fno-var-tracking-assignments)
#   method  - optional; "zkg" (the default) or "clone:<path under ZEEK_DIR>" for a plain git checkout

